R"VG(
# instructions.vg (H-04's second pass): the far future's instructions (to keep the works, to wake the keeper, to live in what they left):
# every step composed of a doing and a place that fit each other, with its reason, so a people that left twenty sets of instructions
# never says the same thing twice; the places are the people's own (their great work, their holy place, their colours and signs, their
# bridges or tunnels or terraces, their gardens, their herds).

genre.instructions (words=34..150)
  {in.head}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.end}
  {in.head}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.end}
  {in.head}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.step}\n{in.end}

in.head (formula people=6)
  To keep {focusword} at {$home} running. For whoever comes.
  How to wake the keeper of {$home}.
  Instructions, left in the hope that someone will need them.
  For the one who finds {$home} empty: what to do, and what not to.
  How to use the water, the light and the doors of {$home}.
  How to live at {$home}, for a day or for a thousand years.
  For the next ones. Read this first; the rest can wait.
  What we would tell you if we were here. We are not, so we wrote it down.
  The care of {$home}, set out plainly.

in.step
  (3 once) {in.go}
  (2 once) {in.leave}
  (2 once) {in.if}
  (1 once) {in.keep}
  (1 once) {in.find}

# ---- a doing and a place --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

in.go
  (3) {in.posture} {in.where}. {in.why}
  (2) {in.speak} {in.whom}. {in.why}
  (1) Follow {in.sense}. {in.why}
  (1) {in.along} {in.path}. {in.why}
  (1) {in.posture} {in.where}, {time.of}. {in.why}
  (1) First, {in.posture.lc} {in.where}. {in.why}

in.posture
  Stand
  Sit
  Wait
  Rest
  Stay a while
  Lie down
  Kneel, if you like,
  Sing, quietly,
in.posture.lc
  stand
  sit
  wait
  rest
  stay a while

in.where (share=0.6)
  in the light at the centre
  beside the pool in the lowest room
  under the dome
  beside the column that hums
  at the door that opens by itself
  on the {colour.holy} stair
  under {motif.over} in the great hall
  in the {fut.green}
  at the foot of {focusword}
  in the room with no corners
  by the window that faces {in.faces}
  where the floor is warm
  in the circle of {colour.holy} stones
  by the spring in the lowest room
  at {holyplace}
  among the {tree} on the upper level
  (links=bridges) on the long bridge, in the middle
  (links=tunnels) in the tunnel where it widens
  (links=arcades) under the arcades
  (links=colonnades) between the columns
  (land=terraced) on the highest terrace
  (land=cliffs) in the gallery cut into the cliff
  (land=stilts) on the platform above the water
  (land=pits) at the bottom of the sunken garden
  (public=courts) in the inner court
  (public=plazas) in the middle of the square
  (light=lines) where the lines on the floor meet
  (light=lamps) under the oldest lamp
in.faces
  {mountain}
  {sun.first}
  (moons>0) {moon}
  {river}
  the sea of {sea}
  the old city

in.speak
  Speak to
  Sing to
  Call out to
  Whisper to
  Say your name to
  Ask about us of
in.whom (share=0.7)
  the wall that is warm
  the column that hums
  the light
  the pool
  the doors
  the room with no corners
  the {~keeper}
  {focusword}
  the {colour.holy} stone by the gate
  the oldest of the machines

in.along
  Follow
  Walk along
  Keep to
  Count your steps along
in.path (share=0.7)
  the line on the floor
  the {colour.holy} stones
  {motif.over} on the walls
  the oldest corridor, which slopes down
  the wall with the names on it
  (light=lines) the light in the floor
  (light=lamps) the lamps
  (links=bridges) the bridges, east to west
  (links=tunnels) the tunnels, downward
  (land=terraced) the terraces, upward
in.sense (share=0.7)
  the sound of water
  the warm air
  the bells, if they are ringing
  the smell of the {fut.green}
  the {bird}, if any are left
  the light, wherever it goes

# ---- what not to do ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

in.leave
  (2) Do not touch {in.touch}. {in.why2}
  (2) Do not wake {in.wake}. {in.why2}
  (2) Do not open {in.open}. {in.why2}
  (1) Do not move {in.move}. {in.why2}
  (1) Do not try to stop {in.stop}. {in.why2}
in.touch (share=0.7)
  the dark panels
  the {colour.mourn} stones
  the column at night
  the glass that is cold
  the {vessel} on the high shelf
  {motif.over} in the lowest room
  the water in the black basin
  {instrument} in the great hall, which is tuned for someone else
  the {craft} workshop's last piece, which is not finished
in.wake (share=0.7)
  the sleepers
  the small machines
  the keeper, whatever happens
  the {herd} in the lower pens, if any are left
  anything in the room with the blue light
  the {bird} nesting in the {fut.gate}; they were here first
  the old ones in the {fut.block}, if you find any; they have earned it
in.open (share=0.7)
  the sealed rooms
  the lowest door
  the {colour.holy} boxes
  the floor where it rings hollow
  the cases in the archive that are marked with {motif.over}
  the {vessel} in the cold store; they are older than they look
in.move (share=0.7)
  the stones in the circle
  the bones in the niches
  the chairs in the {fut.common}
  the {vessel} by the doors
  the {colour.holy} cloths on the long table
  the {tree} in the {fut.green}; they have their reasons for where they are
in.stop (share=0.8)
  the hum
  the water
  the music in the lowest room
  the lights in the evening
  {instrument} in the great hall; it plays itself at {festival}
  the bells of {holyplace}
  the fountains in the {fut.common}
  the slow wheel in the {craft} workshop

# ---- if ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

in.if
  (2) If {in.c.sign}, {in.r.sign}.
  (2) If you are hungry, {in.r.hungry}.
  (1) If you are thirsty, {in.r.thirsty}.
  (1) If you are cold, {in.r.cold}.
  (1) If you are tired, {in.r.tired}.
  (2) If you are {in.c.lonely}, {in.r.lonely}.
  (1) If you hear {in.c.hear}, {in.r.hear}.
  (1) If you want to leave, {in.r.leave}.
in.c.sign
  the hum stops
  the hum changes
  the floor grows warm
  the lights dim
  the light turns red
  the doors do not open
  the bells ring by themselves
  the water rises in the pool
in.r.sign
  wait; it will start again
  sit down where you are and wait, as the {herd} do
  count to {#number} hundred, slowly
  go to the lowest room and sit
  say your name, once
  open your hands and stand still
  do nothing; it is only remembering
in.r.hungry
  ask the wall; it knows where the food is
  go to the {fut.green}; something is always ripe
  eat the {fruit} by the door; they are still good
  look behind the third door; we left {food}
  the store under the {colour.holy} stair is full
in.r.thirsty
  drink from the spring in the lowest room, where the {colour.holy} tiles are
  the water in the {colour.holy} bowls is clean
  ask for water, and {drink} if you like; both will come
  drink from {watersrc}; it was kept clean for you
in.r.cold
  stand by the column that hums, under {motif.over}
  the room with no corners is warm, and smells of {fuel}
  wrap yourself in the {colour.holy} cloth in the chests; it was ours
  light the lamps; they still burn {fuel}
in.r.tired
  sleep in the room with no corners
  lie down anywhere; nothing here will hurt you
  the beds in the {fut.block} are made; we made them
in.c.lonely
  alone
  afraid
  sad
  lost
in.r.lonely
  you are not; we are in the records, and the records will talk to you
  speak, and the walls will answer in our voices
  go to {holyplace} and sit with the names
  sing; we always did
  ask the archive for a story; ask for the long one
in.c.hear
  voices
  singing
  something speak your name
  {instrument}
in.r.hear
  they are ours, recorded; they will not mind you listening
  answer; it is only manners
  follow the sound; it goes somewhere good
  sit down and listen; we played it for whoever came
in.r.leave
  the way out is the way you came in, past the {fut.green}
  go, and leave the doors open behind you
  take something with you, so that something of us goes
  go when you like; we did

# ---- keeping and finding ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

in.keep
  (3) {in.when} {in.keepdo}. {in.why}
  (1) {in.keepdo.cap}, {in.when.lc}. {in.why}
in.when (share=0.8)
  Once a year, at {festival},
  Every morning,
  When the {bird} come back,
  At {festival},
  Every hundred years or so,
  When the hum is low,
  Before you sleep,
  On the longest night,
  When you have time, and you will,
  Once in a while,
in.when.lc
  once a year
  every morning
  at {festival}
  when the hum is low
  when you remember
in.keepdo (share=0.8)
  light the {colour.holy} lamps
  sweep {holyplace}
  feed the {herd} in the lower pens, if any are left
  wind the clock in the great hall
  say the names of the dead at {holyplace}, as many as you can
  water the {tree} on the upper level
  close the shutters on the {fut.block}
  play {fut.game} in the {fut.common}; the pieces are still there
  open the {fut.gate} for an hour, to let the old air out
  sing one of the {festival} songs, any of them
  polish {motif.over} on the great doors
  turn the soil in the {fut.green}
  ring the {#number} bells, by hand
  check the seals on the vault, and say aloud that they are good
  cook {food} in the big kitchen, even if only for yourself
  walk to {focusword} and touch it
in.keepdo.cap
  Light the {colour.holy} lamps
  Sweep {holyplace}
  Wind the clock in the great hall
  Ring the {#number} bells
  Turn the soil in the {fut.green}
in.find
  (3) {in.thing>.t} {be:.t} {in.found}. {in.why}
  (1) If you want {in.want}, look {in.found}. {in.why}
in.thing
  (pl) Our records
  (pl) The tools
  (sing) The map
  (sing) The music
  (pl) The seeds of the {crop}
  (pl) Our names
  (pl) The children's drawings
  (pl) The recipes for {food}
  (sing) The {~book}
  (pl) The keys we kept
  (sing) The cloth we wove
  (pl) The pieces for {fut.game}
in.found (share=0.8)
  behind the {colour.holy} door
  in the cases in the lowest room
  under the floor of the {fut.common}
  in the {craft} workshop, oiled and labelled
  cut into the wall at {holyplace}
  in the vault under {focusword}
  with the machines, who will hand them over if you ask nicely
  in the chests in the {fut.block}
  where the light lines end
  under the {colour.holy} stair
  in the room with no corners, on the left
  on the high shelf in the {fut.green}
in.want
  to know who we were
  something to eat that we made
  to hear us
  to make something
  to know the way out

in.end
  (2) {in.end.a} {in.end.b}
  (1) {in.end.a}
  (1) {in.end.b}
  (1) {in.end.c}
in.end.c (share=0.8)
  Light a lamp at {holyplace} for us, if you think of it.
  If the {herd} are still here, they are yours; be kind to them.
  We kept {festival} here for a very long time; keep it once, for us.
  Tell the machines your name. They have been waiting to learn a new one.
  The {colour.holy} cloth on the table is for you. It was ours.
  When you leave, tell someone about us, if there is anyone to tell.
  Sing something in the {fut.common}. It has been quiet a long time.
  Eat the {fruit} in the {fut.green}. Nobody else will.
in.end.a (share=0.55)
  That is all you need.
  That is everything.
  There is more, but you will find it, as we found the {fruit}.
  If you forget, ask the walls.
  The rest is in the records.
  Do these, and the place will do the rest.
  Nothing else is important.
  The rest you can learn by living here.
  You will make mistakes; the place forgives them.
  We have written more, but this is what matters.
  The machines know the rest; they are only waiting to be asked.
  Everything else is a matter of taste.
  If something is not written here, it does not need doing.
  We did all this for a thousand years. It was not a burden.
  Read this again in a year; it will say something different.
  That is the end of the instructions and the beginning of the rest.
in.end.b (share=0.55 formula)
  The rest will be shown to you.
  You are welcome here.
  Close the doors behind you, for the next one.
  Whoever you are: we left it ready for you.
  Stay as long as you like.
  We hope you like it here. We did.
  {blessing}.
  Be kinder to it than time was.
  The place is yours now; be good to it, and to the {herd}.
  We would have liked to meet you.
  Go well, and come back if you like.
  You will not be the last; leave it as you found it, with {motif.over} on the door.
  Think of us at {festival}, if you keep it.
  We are glad it was you.
)VG"
